 "text": "Hi, how have you been? She's little bigger than a typical six year old, so she probably eats more too. A balanced meal that includes a variety of foods from all the food groups is the way to go. That's easy to do with pouches and single items. A balanced meal comes from mixing things up. A little milk and a piece of toast is a good way to start each morning. A little fruit doesn't hurt either. She' love the coffee. A big cup after she's out bed also helps with night dreams. At this age, yes. Giving her small tasks like pulling things out of the cupboards and setting the table helps too.",
